  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.25\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.25 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.24\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.24 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.23\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.23 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.22\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.22 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.21\n- No functional changes; synchronized with the framework-free MAUI integration sweep.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.20\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.20 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.19\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.19 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.18\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.18 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.17\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.17 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.16\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.16 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.15\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.15 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.14\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.14 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.13\n- Updated to depend on FireForNet.Firebase.Firestore 1.0.1-preview.13, which adds offline-first optimistic writes (opt-in via FirestoreBuilder.OptimisticWrites) and eliminates the proto-to-JSON round-trip on typed model conversion. Offline writes persist via the SQLite backend.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.12\n- Updated to depend on FireForNet.Firebase.Firestore 1.0.1-preview.12, which fixes ObjectDisposedException on SemaphoreSlim.Release() during network disable and UnobservedTaskException from WebChannel receive-loop exceptions during concurrent disposal.",
